WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.480
After "Loki" Episode 4, "The Nexus Event,"&nbsp;
ended with a shocking cliffhanger, the wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.280
for Episode 5 was excruciating. But now the latest&nbsp;
installment, "Journey Into Mystery," has arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.360
and with it, some big questions. Here's&nbsp;
the ending of "Loki" Episode 5, explained.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.080
It's established very quickly — thanks to&nbsp;
a forced confession from Judge Renslayer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.680
Sylvie — that the TVA's pruning batons&nbsp;
don't actually kill Variants. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.920
they transport them to a place in time called the&nbsp;
Void, where they can be vaporized by a malevolent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.200
smoky-force called Alioth . The Void's existence&nbsp;
is obviously a highly-classified TVA secret, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.600
is why Loki didn't learn about it when he was&nbsp;
asking for files from the clerk back in Episode 2.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.760
In Marvel comics, Alioth is closely tied to&nbsp;
a notorious time-traveling villain who many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.400
fans are expecting to see very soon in "Ant-Man&nbsp;
and the Wasp: Quantumania" — Kang the Conqueror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.240
and he's reportedly being played by&nbsp;
"Lovecraft Country" star Jonathan Majors.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.960
The big smoky beast had his own temporal empire&nbsp;
when he was originally introduced back in 1993's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.600
"Avengers: The Terminatrix Objective" #1, but&nbsp;
Kang constructed a time-barrier to keep the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.320
villain out of his own domain, called Chronopolis.&nbsp;
That doesn't sound too dissimilar to what the TVA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.680
has done with Alioth in "Loki" — trapping&nbsp;
the entity in the Void so they can use him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.280
to wipe out pesky Variants and other things&nbsp;
that don't belong in the sacred timeline.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.080
The bulk of the episode follows our main Loki&nbsp;
chatting with the other Variants and discovering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.440
what makes them so different from himself,&nbsp;
all while trying to find a way to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.680
Alioth and figure out who's really behind the&nbsp;
TVA. The episode doesn't rush through things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.800
giving this "God Squad" plenty of time&nbsp;
to bounce off one another, all while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.480
expanding the mythology and development&nbsp;
of everyone's favorite God of Mischief.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.640
Classic Loki explains how he lived past&nbsp;
the events of "Avengers: Infinity War."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.160
He reveals that he conjured an illusion&nbsp;
of himself so exacting that he fooled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.840
Thanos into thinking the decoy was&nbsp;
real, and that he'd killed Loki.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.560
From there, Classic Loki went into hiding as&nbsp;
"inanimate debris." Cowardly and smart — yes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.880
that's classic Loki, alright. But not only&nbsp;
is it an insightful anecdote as to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.320
Lokis are capable of when they put their&nbsp;
mind to it, it's also a clue as to how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.000
vibrantly dressed character will have an&nbsp;
impact in the final fight against Alioth.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.760
It all ends in a big scuffle when a variant&nbsp;
we'll call President Loki shows up with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.440
army of other Variant Lokis from across&nbsp;
the Void's wasteland. However, they all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.600
start betraying each other — because that's&nbsp;
just what Lokis do, isn't it? At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.440
it looks like the small appearance from President&nbsp;
Loki might debunk a few of those theories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.400
suggesting that he's the one behind the TVA. It's&nbsp;
still not impossible, but it's highly unlikely.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.520
They just couldn't stay apart for too long,&nbsp;
could they? Sylvie follows Loki to the Void&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.880
after Renslayer reveals that the Void&nbsp;
is a place at the end of the timeline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.600
That means it's out of harm's way and can't affect&nbsp;
past events. Sylvie's self-pruning shows that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.240
the Variant clearly cares as deeply for the main&nbsp;
Loki as he cares for her. Her main motivation is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.280
finding out who's really behind the TVA, but she's&nbsp;
just not very good at expressing her emotions.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.720
This is something that comes across very&nbsp;
clearly in a touching moment leading up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.440
final battle. While Kid, Classic, and Gator Loki&nbsp;
shelter in a hollowed out building with Mobius,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.440
Loki and Sylvie huddle together in a conjured&nbsp;
blanket while they try to untangle the romantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.200
mess they've created for themselves. It's&nbsp;
clearly the first time Sylvie has ever let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.480
herself be vulnerable with anyone, so&nbsp;
it's quite fitting that she's opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.560
up to an alternate version of herself. But&nbsp;
she even struggles to connect with Loki.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:11.120
"I don't have friends, I don't have anyone."

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.200
Finally, Loki gets his own redemption arc&nbsp;
as he promises not to betray Sylvie. He hugs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.360
Mobius and calls him a friend before the TVA&nbsp;
agent heads back to work to "burn it down."

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.680
Loki and Sylvie head off to face Alioth&nbsp;
themselves while the rest of the God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.680
Squad decides to stay in the Void — after&nbsp;
all, this is their home now. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.600
Sylvie vetoes Loki's simple plan of trying to&nbsp;
stab a smoke monster, and goes with her idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.600
of enchanting the creature into revealing&nbsp;
where and who the person behind the TVA is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.280
However, just because she's been nefariously&nbsp;
murderous up to this point doesn't mean she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.600
can't inspire Loki to have a little faith in&nbsp;
himself. He unlocks his own enchanting abilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.440
just in the nick of time on the battlefield,&nbsp;
with a little encouragement from Sylvie.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.680
Thankfully, Classic Loki decides to give his&nbsp;
life "glorious purpose" by creating a fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.080
Asgard to distract Alioth. It is a brilliant&nbsp;
moment to witness, especially for an older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.280
bitter version of the character, to finally&nbsp;
feel like he's doing something positive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.040
in the timeline rather than constantly&nbsp;
being a villain. His trickery succeeds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.680
but at the cost of his life. However, Classic&nbsp;
Loki points out earlier on that he cheated death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.680
by conjuring a fake version of himself during&nbsp;
the confrontation with Thanos, so who knows?

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.480
Once Alioth is enchanted, the smoke clears to&nbsp;
show a bizarre castle or manor in the middle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.960
a swirling cosmic background. With all the&nbsp;
Kang the Conqueror connections to Alioth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:26.000
is it possible that this is Chronopolis? Alioth&nbsp;
clearly couldn't get inside it. In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.320
Chronopolis lies on the outskirts of limbo and&nbsp;
contains time-points to places under Kang's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.920
control. Will we see Jonathan Majors as Kang next&nbsp;
week, in the "Loki" finale? Only time will tell.

